══ P5 — cold start: the arm's pod deleted (a fresh emptyDir), time to the first ls-remote and the first clone of the 1024 MiB branch ══
  FAIL  forge: P5 cold start NEVER COMPLETED — the successor refused to serve and
        crash-looped (exit 78, 10 restarts). Cause, established from the bucket:
        the snapshot named 55 refs but only 3 packs, and 13 of those refs need
        commits that live only in packs the snapshot had stopped naming. The
        batch log shows those 13 packs named at seq 77 and un-named at seq 127 by
        a fold whose output pack does NOT contain their objects (verified by
        searching its index). NO DATA LOST: all 13 commits are still in the
        bucket in their original packs. The refusal is forge's proof working as
        designed; the defect is the fold. Diagnostic defect alongside it: the
        refusal message printed only fsck's stderr ("HEAD points to an unborn
        branch"), while the real reason ("missing commit ...") goes to stdout and
        was discarded.
  ....  P11 and P10 NOT RUN — the run was stopped once P5 wedged.

